Basic math operations in plain English.

Use core.

Publicly, to find the absolute value of a whole number x, named abs_i64, returning a whole number.
Give back 0 minus x if x is less than 0, otherwise give back x.

Publicly, to find the absolute value of a decimal x, named abs_f64, returning a decimal.
Give back 0.0 if x equals 0.0.
Give back 0.0 minus x if x is less than 0.0, otherwise give back x.

Publicly, to find the smaller of whole numbers a and b, named min_i64, returning a whole number.
Give back a if a is less than b, otherwise give back b.

Publicly, to find the larger of whole numbers a and b, named max_i64, returning a whole number.
Give back a if a is more than b, otherwise give back b.

Publicly, to find the smaller of decimals a and b, named min_f64, returning a decimal.
Give back a if a is less than b, otherwise give back b.

Publicly, to find the larger of decimals a and b, named max_f64, returning a decimal.
Give back a if a is more than b, otherwise give back b.

Publicly, to find the square root of a decimal x, named sqrt, returning a decimal.
Call this as "square root of <x>".
Stop with error "sqrt of negative number" if x is less than 0.0.
Give back 0.0 if x equals 0.0.
Let guess be 1.0.
Set guess to 0.5 times x if x is at least 1.0.
Let iteration be 0.
Until iteration is at least 24, set guess to 0.5 times (guess plus x divided by guess), add 1 to iteration.
Give back guess.

Publicly, to raise a whole number base to a whole number exponent, named pow_i64, returning a whole number.
Give back 0 if exponent is less than 0.
Let result be 1.
Let factor be base.
Let power be exponent.
While power is more than 0, set result to result times factor if power modulo 2 equals 1, set factor to factor times factor, set power to power divided by 2.
Give back result.

Publicly, to clamp a whole number number_to_clamp between a whole number lower_bound and a whole number upper_bound, named clamp_i64, returning a whole number.
Give back lower_bound if number_to_clamp is less than lower_bound.
Give back upper_bound if number_to_clamp is more than upper_bound.
Give back number_to_clamp.
